query:
UPDATE services SET
  faqs = '[{"q":"What types of municipal infrastructure does Discount Drain work on?","a":"We work on sanitary sewer mains, storm sewer systems, manholes, water mains, service laterals, catch basins, and drainage outfalls. We also handle road culvert replacements and large-scale excavation projects for municipalities and conservation authorities."},{"q":"Can you line a sewer main without excavating the road?","a":"Yes. Our cured-in-place pipe lining process installs a new structural liner inside the existing pipe through access points at manholes. No road cutting is required in most cases. The liner cures in place and restores the pipe to full structural and hydraulic capacity."},{"q":"How long does a CIPP sewer liner last?","a":"A properly installed CIPP liner has a design life of 50 years or more. The liner is seamless, resistant to root intrusion, and eliminates the joints and cracks that allow groundwater infiltration into the sewer system."},{"q":"What is inflow and infiltration, and why does it matter for municipalities?","a":"Inflow is stormwater that enters the sanitary sewer system through illegal connections, open manholes, or damaged pipes. Infiltration is groundwater that seeps in through cracks and failed joints. Both increase the volume of flow that wastewater treatment plants must handle, which raises operating costs. Lining and manhole restoration programs reduce inflow and infiltration significantly."},{"q":"Do you handle emergency water main breaks?","a":"Yes. We offer emergency response for water main breaks with our own excavation equipment. We do not subcontract the excavation, which means we can respond and begin work faster than contractors who need to arrange third-party equipment."},{"q":"Can you work within municipal right-of-way and road allowances?","a":"Yes. We are fully insured, WSIB compliant, and experienced working within municipal road allowances. We coordinate with the municipality on traffic control, utility locates, and permit requirements before any work begins."},{"q":"What documentation do you provide after a municipal job?","a":"We provide pre and post camera inspection footage, as-built records for any new installations, and written reports on the condition of the infrastructure before and after our work. Documentation requirements vary by project and we work to meet whatever the municipality specifies."},{"q":"How do you handle traffic control during road-based work?","a":"We work with certified traffic control personnel and follow the Ontario Traffic Manual requirements for all road-based work. Traffic management plans are prepared in advance and submitted to the municipality or road authority before work begins."},{"q":"Do you work with conservation authorities and provincial agencies?","a":"Yes. We have experience working with conservation authorities on drainage and culvert projects that fall within regulated areas. We are familiar with the permit requirements and environmental conditions that apply to work near watercourses and wetlands in Ontario."},{"q":"What areas do you serve for municipal work?","a":"We serve municipalities and public agencies across London and Southwestern Ontario, including the City of London, Middlesex County, Elgin County, Oxford County, and surrounding townships. Contact us to discuss your project and service area."}]'
WHERE slug = 'municipal-services';

